    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897">

                <pb facs="0835" n="823" xml:id="pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">300.115(39) Young, Inc., Daniel F./3:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-13T18:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. There have been presented to the Department by Daniel F. Young,
                    Incorporated, affidavits executed by buyers of the following mentioned cargo
                    loaded on board the Latvian steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Andrejs
                        Kalnins</hi> which is understood to be ready to sail from Riga but is
                    detained on account of uncertainty with respect to the ultimate destination of
                    such cargo. Each affidavit states in substantially the same language that the
                    commodities in question are for consumption in the United States and will in no
                    circumstances and in no form be re-exported from the United States. Articles
                    covered by such affidavits are as follows: [The list of articles is here
                    omitted.]</p>
                <p>Endeavor to utilize the foregoing information with a view to facilitating the
                    shipment of the indicated commodities as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
